  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high: human absolute-bioavailability records for polar ribonucleoside analogs (viramidine 66.1%, lamivudine 86%, zalcitabine 80%) and L3 oral exposure records for ribavirin and didanosine support F ≥ 20% for a ribose-containing nucleoside; L2/L3 low-F records for other species/analogs and the query's extreme polarity and unusual N-amino linkage add uncertainty but do not provide affirmative evidence for F < 20%, so high is retained with moderate confidence."
